## Crime AKS application secrets

Crime AKS has two secret integrations - they are selected per-service:

- **HashiCorp Vault:** Ansible Hashicorp Vault plugin is used to retrieve secrets using `lookup('vault', ...)` expressions in [cpp-aks-deploy values files](https://github.com/hmcts/cpp-aks-deploy/tree/main/ansible/group_vars), they read secrets while the deployment values are rendered. The ADO pipeline receives Vault connection details from its live or non-live variable group.
- **Azure Key Vault:** a service with `secretProvider.create: true` declares Key Vault secret mappings in its values. The shared [springboot-app](https://github.com/hmcts/cpp-helm-chart/blob/main/springboot-app/templates/secretProviderClass.yaml) and [wildfly-app](https://github.com/hmcts/cpp-helm-chart/blob/main/wildfly-app/templates/secretProviderClass.yaml) charts create a Secrets Store CSI `SecretProviderClass` so the pod can receive the mapped secrets at runtime.

Existing services (such as CCM) use both mechanisms - required secret, identity and access must exist before deployment.

When working with secrets you should only store the lookup expressions or key vault mappings in the code - never actual secret values.
